- op: discuss  # 2d6f
  at: '2026-10-01T01:37:40Z'  # 2d6f
  by: agent  # 2d6f
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2d6f
  clock: 3  # 2d6f
  nonce: 2d6f  # 2d6f
  message: "SCOPE CLARIFICATION 2026-09-30 (owner asked): this row does NOT ask for a per-PR gate. WI-ratuv was deliberately kept out of per-PR CI because building the map takes ~13m40s (script header; owner-approved design, PR #717) and was meant to ride the twice-daily scheduled full-suite. That decision stands. The defect is only WHICH scheduled job it was wired into: the GitHub copy (schedule off since 07-23) instead of the live Woodpecker copy. The fix adds one step to .woodpecker/full-suite.yml's self-tree-validation step, which already builds /tmp/self-tree.json, so the added cost on the cron is seconds. The \"test pinning it\" is a cheap unit test that reads the Woodpecker YAML and asserts the step is present (like tests/test_ci_self_claims_gate_scope.py), not a test that runs the gate."  # 2d6f
- op: discuss  # 9971
  at: '2026-10-03T06:41:59Z'  # 9971
  by: agent  # 9971
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9971
  clock: 4  # 9971
  nonce: '9971'  # 9971
  message: "PREMISE AUDIT 2026-10-03 (owner-requested; read-only, reproduced at dev 3abedae588 on small fixtures). CURRENT; the class is wider than the named gate. Full step-by-step diff of .github/workflows/full-suite.yml vs .woodpecker/full-suite.yml:\n1. The test-only-reachability ratchet (this item): only in the GHA file (now :299-318); no .woodpecker/ step and no test pins it. The GHA `::warning::` syntax needs a plain echo when ported.\n2. PER-PACKAGE COVERAGE IN ISOLATION (not in this item): GHA runs each package's tests alone with --cov on that package's src at 100%. Woodpecker test-all-packages (:103-113) runs all packages in one pass with all --cov paths, so a line covered only by ANOTHER package's tests counts. Per-PR woodpecker.yml (:516-554) and nightly use the same union, so no live CI enforces AGENTS.md's \"tests live in the same package as the code they cover\"; only local check-package-coverage does. It has bitten before: WI-tubuv (core 99% in isolation), WI-dojuh (cli.py uncovered in core isolation). Partly tracked by WI-kahar (todo_soft P4).\n3. MIS-PINNED TEETH TEST: tests/test_full_suite_coverage_teeth.py:22 says `# covers: .woodpecker/full-suite.yml`, but every assertion reads FULL_SUITE = .github/workflows/full-suite.yml (:29). It pins the dormant file, the same class as this item.\nGHA-only items that are NOT gates: SHA-already-tested/docs-only skips, *-retry jobs, aggregate stop-the-line, coverage badge, last-green-sha marker, full-suite/aggregate status (nothing reads it). Nightly: no gate missing. Recommendation: widen the statement to \"a gate that exists only in .github/ runs nowhere\" and track 2 and 3 here or as siblings (not done; owner/agent choice)."  # 9971
