  clock: 5  # 94be
  nonce: 94be  # 94be
  message: "FROM WI-kabaf (2026-10-03, branch jgstern-agent/fix/kabaf, 1f4c88c755, not pushed). Bears on this row's class sweep, which compared full-suite and nightly but not the per-PR pair. One per-PR data point: WI-kabaf's defect (manifest counted by grep -c \"^packages/\") existed ONLY in the dormant .github/workflows/ci.yml; the live .woodpecker/woodpecker.yml pytest step counts the SELECTED_TESTS section correctly. I did not diff ci.yml against woodpecker.yml step by step, so this is NOT a statement that the per-PR pair has no gate missing from .woodpecker/. Possible merge contact: the kabaf branch adds tests/test_ci_github_manifest_count.py, which parametrizes over every .woodpecker/*.yml and fails if a line counts a manifest with a prefix-keyed grep -c; it edits no .woodpecker/ file."  # 94be
- op: discuss  # 9165
  at: '2026-10-03T08:07:28Z'  # 9165
  by: agent  # 9165
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9165
  clock: 6  # 9165
  nonce: '9165'  # 9165
  message: "WORK DONE 2026-10-03 (concurrent run, branch jgstern-agent/fix/hokin, LOCAL, not pushed): cfd14717a0 (port + tests), 71f327c4bc (baseline re-freeze, owner to ratify; separable).\n\n1. PORT. .woodpecker/full-suite.yml self-tree-validation now runs `python scripts/check-test-only-reachability --map /tmp/self-tree.json` after the map build, scheduled-only (not per-PR). Exit 2 warns and passes. Both self-map ratchets run regardless of the other's result (rc captured under set -e) and the step fails if either failed, so neither masks the other. Step name unchanged.\n2. PIN. tests/test_check_test_only_reachability_ci_wiring.py runs the step's own commands under /bin/sh -e with a stub python (reach, unconditional, exit 1 reds, exit 2 passes with a warning, no masking, failed map build stops the step). Mutations: gate line deleted -> 7 red; rc not captured -> 2 red; final exit deleted -> 4 red; all nonzero treated as infra -> 2 red.\n3. TEETH TEST (premise audit item 3). tests/test_full_suite_coverage_teeth.py now reads .woodpecker/: --cov-fail-under=100 on every packages/*/tests/ pytest step (full-suite + nightly), not swallowed, no failure: ignore / when; per-PR no-data branch in woodpecker.yml. Mutations red; the OLD file stayed 4/4 green under the same mutations (vacuous, as the audit said). Same mis-pin fixed in tests/test_workflow_cli_invocation.py (scanned .github only; its pattern could not match a YAML `- cmd` item).\n4. FIRST LIVE-EQUIVALENT RUN (local, via the board, map of this worktree at 62602239c6, 5m05s, 280 MB): exit 1, 21 new keys + 3 drained. Adjudicated per key in 71f327c4bc's message: 6 called from scripts/ (gate scope, filed WI-modip-barab-himus-gaduj-gojip-hizuj-lutor-sihit), 3 test hooks / test-run gates, 4 declaration-table queries, 8 UNWIRED (filed WI-mifup-gumim-jokop-litup-pogud-govaj-pinag-bonut). After re-freeze: exit 0. Code mutation (new paths.py function called only by a new test, fresh map): exit 1 naming exactly that key.\n5. CLASS (fix shape step 4): premise audit already diffed full-suite and nightly; the per-package isolation gap (audit item 2) filed as WI-sagar-tafan-gogon-gajul-rafif-matub-fifar-mizul. Swept tests that pin dormant .github files: test_check_mypy_ratchet_blocking.py reads only ci.yml, but the live Woodpecker mypy step is pinned separately by test_smart_test_mypy_gate.py (strict + not failure: ignore), so it is redundant, not a live gap. Not filed. Seen, not fixed: woodpecker.yml:570 comment still says the mypy step is failure: ignore; :128-133 say it was removed.\n\nNOT CHECKED: a real Woodpecker firing (no cron here; the /bin/sh -e model is the test's claim about the runner). The local map was built on Python 3.12 with every package importable; CI builds on 3.11 with core+mainstream+common+extended1+tracker installed. Whether the two maps give the same cohort was NOT measured, so the cron's first firing may still differ from the local exit 0. Run ci-debug cron-status after the first firing that includes this."  # 9165
