- op: discuss  # b6a7
  at: '2026-10-03T09:41:12Z'  # b6a7
  by: agent  # b6a7
  actor: jgstern_agent  # b6a7
  clock: 8  # b6a7
  nonce: b6a7  # b6a7
  message: "Wired in PR #1408. Status pending_validation, not satisfied: the scheduled full-suite has not fired on it yet. Satisfy after `ci-debug cron-status` shows self-tree-validation green with the ratchet running.\n\nINV-hokin: the WI-ratuv test-only-reachability ratchet now runs in the live scheduled pipeline, `.woodpecker/full-suite.yml` step `self-tree-validation`, on the map that step builds. It is not per-PR, per the owner's ruling.\n\nBehavioral evidence:\n- `tests/test_check_test_only_reachability_ci_wiring.py` runs the step's commands under `/bin/sh -e`. The step goes red on gate exit 1 and passes with a warning on exit 2. The two self-map ratchets cannot hide each other. Four YAML mutations each turned it red.\n- Run locally through the board against a current self-map, `scripts/check-test-only-reachability` exits 0 with the adjudicated baseline. A code mutation (a production function called only by a test) gives exit 1 naming exactly that key.\n- The mis-pinned teeth test (premise audit item 3) and `test_workflow_cli_invocation.py` now read `.woodpecker/`. The old versions stayed green under the same mutations that turn the new ones red.\n\nWhat this closure does not assert:\n- That the general statement holds for every gate. The full-suite and nightly diff was done by the premise audit, and per-package isolation is WI-sagar.\n- That the cron's first firing is green. CI's Python version and install set differ from the local run; check with `ci-debug cron-status`.\n\nResiduals filed: WI-mifup (8 unwired functions), WI-modip (scripts/ callers count as test-only), WI-sagar (no live per-package isolation).\n\n\nOWNER RATIFIED (2026-10-03) the baseline re-freeze in commit a2261d0770 (+21/-3, adjudicated in its commit message): 13 keys not dead (6 scripts/-only callers, 3 intended test callers, 4 test-only lookups; the gate blind spot is WI-modip), 8 truly unwired keys tracked on WI-mifup."  # b6a7
